-- title:
--   Chart image lies in the swap-fixed subring of the crossing model
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and $\pi \in W$. Write $R_\pi = \mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W / (X_0X_1 - C(\pi))$ for the crossing model `UVCrossingModel W π`, the quotient of the two-variable formal power series ring over $W$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \pi$. Two maps into $R_\pi$ and one subring of it are involved. First, `chartHom π` is the ring homomorphism $W[[T]] \to R_\pi$ obtained by substituting for the single variable the element `sAmbient` of $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W$ (the substitution being admissible by `hasSubst_sAmbient W`) and then passing to the quotient. Second, `crossingSwap π` is the ring automorphism of $R_\pi$ induced by the involution `uvSwapEquiv` of the ambient power series ring interchanging the two variables, which carries the ideal $(X_0X_1 - \pi)$ to itself. Finally, `fixedSubring π` is the equaliser subring of `crossingSwap π` and the identity, i.e. $\{x \in R_\pi : \mathrm{crossingSwap}\,\pi\,(x) = x\}$. The assertion is the inclusion of subrings: the image of `chartHom π` is contained in `fixedSubring π`.
--
--   This is the subring-level form of the statement that the symmetric chart of the crossing model $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$ factors through the branch-exchange involution, the local algebraic counterpart of the involution interchanging the two components of a degenerate fibre. It is used in the analysis of the fixed subring, in particular by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.range_chartHom_eq_fixedSubring`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.range_chartHom_eq_fixedSubring) and by the statements producing normal forms for invariant elements.
